std.fs — File system operations
================================

Functions for querying and manipulating the file system:
stat, readdir, exists, mkdir, remove, rename, etc.

All functions are `extern` — backed by the host runtime.

    module std.fs


Types
-----

### FileStat

Metadata about a file or directory.

    struct FileStat
        size: i64
        mode: int
        mtime: i64
        is_dir: bool
        is_file: bool

### DirEntry

A single directory entry returned by `readdir`.

    struct DirEntry
        name: string
        is_dir: bool


Functions
---------

### stat

Return metadata about a file.

    extern stat(path: string) -> FileStat

### readdir

List entries in a directory.

    extern readdir(path: string) -> []DirEntry

### exists

Check whether a path exists.

    extern exists(path: string) -> bool

### is_dir

Check whether a path is a directory.

    extern is_dir(path: string) -> bool

### mkdir

Create a directory. Returns 0 on success.

    extern mkdir(path: string) -> int

### mkdirs

Create a directory and all parent directories.

    extern mkdirs(path: string) -> int

### remove

Remove a file or empty directory.

    extern remove(path: string) -> int

### rename

Rename a file or directory.

    extern rename(old_path: string, new_path: string) -> int

### getcwd

Return the current working directory.

    extern getcwd() -> string

### read_file

Read an entire file into a string.

    extern read_file(path: string) -> string

### write_file

Write a string to a file, replacing its contents.

    extern write_file(path: string, data: string) -> int
